WEBVTT

00:28.700 --> 00:31.570
Kacchan, let's turn back.

00:32.460 --> 00:33.890
What're you saying, Wataru?

00:34.260 --> 00:38.930
My mum said that if you don't see a ghost
before you're 20, you'll never see one.

00:39.860 --> 00:42.730
Isn't it okay if we never see one?

00:43.500 --> 00:44.530
You think?

00:45.580 --> 00:48.530
Wouldn't it be boring to live without seeing
any ghosts?

00:49.220 --> 00:51.170
You don't want to see them, Wataru?

00:51.620 --> 00:53.330
There's no such thing as ghosts!

00:53.780 --> 00:57.130
In fact, the whole thing about how
this building is haunted is probably just...

01:15.020 --> 01:16.890
There's no such thing as...

01:17.020 --> 01:20.250
But they say that the new guy in Class 2
saw a ghost here!

01:23.100 --> 01:24.850
I'm sorry!

01:38.740 --> 01:40.090
Huh? What...

02:07.020 --> 02:08.050
Aya?

02:14.020 --> 02:16.480
Aya, is that really you?

02:21.140 --> 02:23.770
Yeah, I guess it's still the first one.

02:28.060 --> 02:29.040
It's mine.

03:04.460 --> 03:06.330
Hey, Wataru. Sorry. This cat...

03:06.460 --> 03:08.570
Kacchan, just now, this guy...

03:08.700 --> 03:09.650
Huh? What?

03:09.780 --> 03:12.770
He, like, whooshed into that door leading
to the skies. See? Over there!

03:13.060 --> 03:14.410
- Huh?
- Wait. What?

03:47.580 --> 03:48.800
I'm gonna be late!

03:48.940 --> 03:49.970
Good morning, sleepyhead!

03:50.100 --> 03:51.570
You could have woken me up!

03:51.700 --> 03:53.930
Can I have this? Oh, it's hot! It's hot!

03:54.060 --> 03:56.850
I'm not very pleased
with this walking around while eating.

03:57.220 --> 03:58.250
But...

03:58.380 --> 04:00.370
Were you not able to sleep?

04:01.340 --> 04:03.690
Isn't it that he was playing around
late at night?

04:04.220 --> 04:06.810
I was doing my homework! Bye!

04:08.020 --> 04:10.480
- Hurry up, Wataru!
- Sorry!

04:12.700 --> 04:15.160
I bet you couldn't sleep
after what you saw yesterday.

04:15.380 --> 04:19.610
Yeah, but no! Seriously!
What I saw was a kid, totally normal!

04:20.100 --> 04:21.930
And then he disappeared
into this huge entrance.

04:22.540 --> 04:25.210
Wish I could see a ghost like you got to.

04:25.940 --> 04:27.890
I'm saying you're wrong!

04:28.380 --> 04:31.690
That was definitely no ghost.

04:32.700 --> 04:34.290
It was a human!

04:38.420 --> 04:40.450
Wataru, look. That guy over there.

04:40.620 --> 04:41.600
Huh?

04:41.740 --> 04:44.970
The new student in Class 2,
who said he saw ghosts.

04:52.220 --> 04:54.170
Hey, Ashikawa-kun!

04:57.460 --> 04:59.210
He is a flirt.

04:59.340 --> 05:03.930
- But all the girls are saying that he's hot.
- Ashikawa-kun! Please say something.

05:04.060 --> 05:06.770
- Don't ask him that all of a sudden!
- Kacchan! It's him!

05:09.900 --> 05:15.450
Was it you who entered the ghost building
without our permission?

05:18.500 --> 05:23.650
That place is reserved for us
sixth-grader Ghost Hunters only.

05:26.620 --> 05:30.210
You still believe in ghosts?
Even after becoming a sixth-grader?

05:33.060 --> 05:34.970
I'll go get the teacher!

05:43.380 --> 05:44.520
Where're you looking?

05:45.660 --> 05:49.330
- You'd better not be ignoring me!
- Stop that!

05:49.460 --> 05:50.440
Ishioka!

05:50.580 --> 05:53.370
Return to your own classroom this instant!

05:53.860 --> 05:56.570
If the teacher hadn't come,
you would have...

05:56.700 --> 05:59.770
Don't be going into my building again!
And don't you forget it!

06:06.660 --> 06:07.640
Amazing.

06:07.780 --> 06:09.450
- Let's go, Wataru.
- Yeah.

06:22.260 --> 06:24.850
Dad! You're early today, huh?

06:25.220 --> 06:26.770
Oh, yeah! Listen to this!

06:26.900 --> 06:30.490
There's this new guy in the next class
and he's really cool!

06:30.620 --> 06:32.410
- Wataru.
- Huh?

06:33.380 --> 06:35.940
I'm leaving this home.

06:36.700 --> 06:39.490
I decided to live with someone
other than your mother.

06:40.140 --> 06:41.090
We're home!

06:41.220 --> 06:43.490
- I'm so hungry!
- So hungry!

06:44.860 --> 06:48.730
Oh! I was so shocked! That's the first time
I've heard you tell a joke!

06:49.300 --> 06:51.810
You can eat dinner at home today, all right?

06:51.980 --> 06:55.890
Wataru, you're already a fifth-grader.
You should understand what I'm saying.

07:00.780 --> 07:02.090
Dad! Wait!

07:04.540 --> 07:06.170
- Mum!
- Hey, Wataru.

07:10.100 --> 07:13.610
Dad's gonna leave!
Don't you need to run after him?

07:14.260 --> 07:16.690
Why? He always goes on business trips.

07:16.820 --> 07:21.210
No! He said he was going to live
with a woman other than you.

07:22.540 --> 07:24.610
Isn't that obviously a joke?

07:25.420 --> 07:27.720
You know that Dad dislikes jokes!

07:35.340 --> 07:36.810
Mum, I'll hold it for you.

07:37.340 --> 07:38.450
It's heavy.

07:38.580 --> 07:39.850
It's fine, it's fine!

07:48.860 --> 07:49.970
Dad!

08:14.380 --> 08:17.010
And he shoots!

08:20.820 --> 08:24.570
- And he scores!
- The athlete Ogawa's brilliant free kick!

08:24.700 --> 08:27.530
Idiot. What're you gonna do
without the goalkeeper?

08:27.660 --> 08:28.610
Sorry.

08:28.740 --> 08:30.770
You feel sorry now? New kid.

08:31.460 --> 08:34.410
Your eyes are so annoying!

08:35.660 --> 08:37.850
I've gotta help him! I've gotta help him!

08:38.100 --> 08:39.080
I've gotta help him!

08:40.900 --> 08:41.880
Who's there?

08:43.500 --> 08:46.450
Who're you? A friend of his?

08:46.780 --> 08:47.810
That's mean!

08:48.140 --> 08:50.440
This is getting interesting.

08:50.980 --> 08:53.250
"That's mean!" he says!

08:55.700 --> 08:58.690
You've got to at least do this to be mean.

09:04.540 --> 09:05.970
No looking elsewhere!

09:06.140 --> 09:07.170
Ishioka-kun!

09:12.340 --> 09:13.400
You brat!

09:16.060 --> 09:18.290
King of the Underworld,

09:18.900 --> 09:21.770
I pray thee based on our covenant.

09:22.820 --> 09:23.850
What is this?

09:24.180 --> 09:27.290
Bring about eternal sleep upon my enemies.

09:27.540 --> 09:29.840
Give them the curse of melting ice!

09:30.940 --> 09:35.530
Sakitose! Helgis! Metose! Helgitose!

09:35.660 --> 09:38.090
Come out!
Daughter of Darkness, Bardarone!

10:30.420 --> 10:31.450
Thanks.

10:40.060 --> 10:45.050
Ishioka's gang is rough and no one
likes them, but to go that far...

10:45.580 --> 10:48.450
That monster I saw just now.
Was it really you?

10:49.660 --> 10:53.770
They were getting in my way, so I made sure
they could never get near again.

10:57.780 --> 11:02.170
Then what was that entrance?
The one that appeared at the ghost building.

11:09.180 --> 11:10.490
What?

11:11.180 --> 11:14.170
It burns!
Looks like I have a cut in my mouth.

11:14.420 --> 11:17.090
Yeah, 'cause they really are merciless.

11:18.820 --> 11:19.850
It doesn't burn?

11:21.780 --> 11:22.890
It really burns!

11:30.860 --> 11:32.080
You...

11:33.180 --> 11:36.800
Since you have nothing to do with me,
you should have left me alone.

11:37.220 --> 11:39.450
You're a regular busybody, huh?

11:40.460 --> 11:44.930
But I'm grateful for what you did.

11:47.220 --> 11:48.250
Yeah.

11:58.740 --> 12:03.450
Oh, so the rumor that you saw ghosts
was just made up by someone.

12:03.580 --> 12:08.570
Probably it just came about
'cause of how often I go to that building.

12:14.220 --> 12:17.330
Hey, hey.
What's on the other side of that entrance?

12:18.100 --> 12:20.050
You really ask a lot of questions.

12:20.180 --> 12:23.850
I'm not your daddy, so it's not like
I have an answer to everything.

12:24.060 --> 12:26.440
I don't call him "Daddy".

12:27.420 --> 12:29.370
What about you? Who's Aya?

12:30.420 --> 12:32.800
I know! It's the girl you have a crush on!

12:33.620 --> 12:35.130
Wait, you're leaving?

12:35.260 --> 12:40.170
I don't have all the time in the world that I
can hang around with carefree kids like you.

12:41.460 --> 12:43.170
That's my line!

12:43.580 --> 12:49.250
I'm not so carefree that I can hang around
with carefree kids like you!

12:50.140 --> 12:53.090
Is that all you got?

12:53.540 --> 12:55.730
Shut up! You wouldn't understand!

12:56.420 --> 12:58.770
Just then, my father walked out.

12:59.020 --> 13:01.370
So then I...

13:01.540 --> 13:04.850
So I'm not a carefree kid!

13:06.140 --> 13:09.920
So what about it? With just a divorce,

13:12.380 --> 13:17.010
if you want to see him,
you can see him whenever you want.

13:18.780 --> 13:20.210
Shut up! What?

13:23.020 --> 13:26.450
Ashikawa! Ashikawa! Ashikawa!

13:31.220 --> 13:33.130
Destiny will be changed.

13:38.420 --> 13:41.770
If you go beyond the entrance,
you can change your destiny.

13:42.700 --> 13:44.050
Your wish will be fulfilled.

13:46.900 --> 13:52.330
If you make a mistake, there are no returns.
But I will go.

13:52.660 --> 13:56.440
Did you get your wish fulfilled already?
Ashikawa!

13:57.020 --> 14:00.640
See you. This is where we part, Mitani.

14:30.780 --> 14:31.840
I'm back.

14:43.020 --> 14:47.250
Mum! Mum! What happened?
What happened!

14:48.060 --> 14:52.410
Mum! Mum! Wake up! Mum!

14:53.860 --> 14:55.730
- Doctor!
- Is she conscious?

14:56.100 --> 14:58.850
- No!
- Open her airway! Send her to ER 3!

14:58.980 --> 14:59.960
Yes, sir!

15:02.860 --> 15:03.810
Mum.

15:11.580 --> 15:16.370
Destiny will be changed. If I go past
the entrance, my wish will be fulfilled.

15:16.940 --> 15:17.970
Mum.

16:20.860 --> 16:22.730
This type of destiny is wrong!

16:25.460 --> 16:26.410
Mum.

16:31.740 --> 16:36.170
Ashikawa! I'll go, too!
To that world beyond this door!

16:36.900 --> 16:41.210
I'm gonna change it. With this hand of mine,
I will change my destiny!

17:34.260 --> 17:36.850
Wataru? Calm down, Wataru.

17:38.500 --> 17:41.130
- Huh?
- You haven't fallen, see?

17:46.500 --> 17:47.450
You're right.

17:47.780 --> 17:49.210
Listen carefully, Wataru.

17:49.660 --> 17:53.610
You must go to the Test of Courage Cave.

17:53.820 --> 17:55.970
Cave? Why?

17:56.620 --> 17:59.080
It's a process necessary for travelers.

17:59.740 --> 18:04.530
It's okay. I'm sure that you'll be able
to come back. You can do it!

18:05.140 --> 18:06.730
Wait! You are...

18:14.900 --> 18:18.010
Take care of your life
while you have your courage tested.

18:18.140 --> 18:20.890
For a question, an answer!
For an answer, a question!

18:22.820 --> 18:25.530
Monk is yawning!

18:26.300 --> 18:31.130
The way to go home will end.
You won't solve it in 1,000 years.

19:01.900 --> 19:04.570
I believe in the Goddess of Destiny.

19:04.700 --> 19:08.290
I am the embodiment of dawn in the East.

19:08.820 --> 19:12.930
Traveler, do you quest to attain bravery?

19:14.340 --> 19:16.850
Bravery?

19:19.100 --> 19:22.210
Do you quest to attain wisdom?

19:22.420 --> 19:23.370
Wisdom?

19:24.980 --> 19:27.410
Do you quest to attain strength?

19:30.220 --> 19:32.370
Do you quest to attain joy?

19:33.100 --> 19:35.810
- Bravery!
- Wisdom!

19:35.940 --> 19:38.450
- Strength!
- Joy!

19:39.180 --> 19:40.770
- Do you wish for it?
- Do you wish for it?

19:40.900 --> 19:42.530
- Do you wish for it?
- Do you wish for it?

19:42.660 --> 19:43.770
- Do you wish for it?
- Do you wish for it?

19:43.900 --> 19:44.960
- Do you wish for it?
- Do you wish for it?

19:45.100 --> 19:47.400
- Do you wish for it?
- Do you wish for it?

19:47.540 --> 19:49.170
Please give me them all!

20:26.980 --> 20:30.250
Just try to run away from me
and return to the woods.

20:42.020 --> 20:43.160
The exit! The exit!

20:52.740 --> 20:55.490
What is this? It isn't an exit?

21:13.500 --> 21:15.730
No, no, it's wrong again!

21:24.460 --> 21:27.770
What? There's no exit
even after opening all the doors!

21:29.900 --> 21:32.330
How am I supposed to get back with this?

21:45.340 --> 21:49.010
A way home, a road home. What is it?

21:53.380 --> 21:57.530
An exit! An exit! An exit! A road home!

21:57.660 --> 22:01.250
An exit! Where is it? The exit!

22:01.980 --> 22:03.010
It's not working...

22:05.580 --> 22:10.970
Frog... Frog... Frog...
Oh! The way home is the frog!

22:12.620 --> 22:13.600
All right!

22:35.340 --> 22:37.250
- Four minutes and 55 seconds.
- Huh?

22:39.980 --> 22:44.810
The travelers before you
figured out the riddle in 50 seconds.

22:51.780 --> 22:54.770
You took a whole lot more time
than Mitsuru.

22:54.940 --> 22:58.560
Mitsuru? Do you know Ashikawa, sir?

22:58.740 --> 22:59.690
"Sir"?

23:01.940 --> 23:06.330
My name is Rau. You can call me Monk Rau.

23:06.820 --> 23:08.930
Monk. Monk Rau.

23:09.420 --> 23:12.450
Monk. Monk Rau.

23:12.780 --> 23:15.570
Good. It's important
to add the word "Monk".

23:15.700 --> 23:17.170
Thank you, Monk Rau.

23:19.140 --> 23:21.810
New traveler, Wataru.

23:21.940 --> 23:22.890
Yes.

23:27.860 --> 23:29.570
Here's the result!

23:32.700 --> 23:34.450
Special talents, zero.

23:34.900 --> 23:35.930
- Zero, zero!
- Zero, zero!

23:36.060 --> 23:37.970
Physical strength is barely average.

23:38.100 --> 23:39.050
- Average, average!
- Average, average!

23:39.220 --> 23:40.490
Courage is of the lowest rank.

23:40.700 --> 23:42.170
- Lowest, lowest!
- Lowest, lowest!

23:44.140 --> 23:46.810
Your total score is 35 points.

23:47.460 --> 23:50.250
For now I will give you the gear
of a trainee of bravery.

24:02.020 --> 24:04.090
What? What is this?

24:05.020 --> 24:08.130
Oh, you don't know anything about this?
Oh, well.

24:08.620 --> 24:12.240
The Goddess of Destiny grants one wish
to travelers like you

24:12.380 --> 24:17.770
who come to Vision from the mortal world.

24:18.180 --> 24:21.610
A goddess grants a wish?

24:24.100 --> 24:27.690
How can I get to the Goddess of Destiny?

24:28.820 --> 24:30.530
Look at your Brave One's sword.

24:30.700 --> 24:31.730
Brave One's sword?

24:32.060 --> 24:33.010
Yes.

24:33.180 --> 24:37.410
When you place a gemstone
into each of those holes,

24:37.540 --> 24:39.970
you can climb up the Tower of Fortune.

24:40.620 --> 24:44.160
There you would find
the Goddess of Destiny.

25:01.780 --> 25:02.840
This?

25:02.980 --> 25:06.330
That gem is a present to you, Traveler.

25:06.460 --> 25:10.570
- Monk Rau! I still have another question!
- Go, trainee of bravery!

25:11.020 --> 25:15.570
Where are the remaining four?

25:23.420 --> 25:26.610
Save me, Monk Rau!

25:30.580 --> 25:31.770
Please?

25:45.180 --> 25:50.200
It would have been so much nicer to be a
magician like Ashikawa instead of a trainee.

25:55.340 --> 25:59.370
With magic, you could just fly to the town.

26:03.140 --> 26:04.250
A dog?

26:05.660 --> 26:07.130
What a strange shape!

26:07.260 --> 26:10.690
Rover! Spot! What is your name?

26:11.500 --> 26:13.370
Maybe it's Loose Screw!

26:18.220 --> 26:19.170
No!

26:20.060 --> 26:21.200
Just kidding.

26:22.260 --> 26:24.640
What about your father and mother?

26:26.380 --> 26:27.730
This way?

26:35.740 --> 26:38.730
Save me! Monk Rau!

26:46.380 --> 26:49.970
Even if I am just a trainee, I'm a Brave One!

27:07.660 --> 27:11.650
Why am I running away
even though I am a Brave One?

27:18.980 --> 27:23.490
You're one with good luck.
This area is wolf robots' territory.

27:24.020 --> 27:25.930
Lizard!

27:52.260 --> 27:53.570
As if!

27:54.060 --> 27:57.890
This animal is called darbada.
First time seeing one like it?

27:58.020 --> 27:58.970
Yes.

27:59.380 --> 28:01.810
There's no need to be scared.

28:01.940 --> 28:03.490
You're the scarier one.

28:03.620 --> 28:07.010
If you rub behind his ears a bit like this,
he likes it a lot.

28:11.940 --> 28:14.050
He's a cute thing, huh?

28:14.180 --> 28:17.410
But really, I'm impressed that you got here
from Irda Empire.

28:17.540 --> 28:20.650
- Empire?
- You don't even know Irda Empire?

28:20.900 --> 28:22.890
Hey, hey.

28:23.660 --> 28:25.610
Hey, kid, you can't be...

28:25.980 --> 28:26.930
Yes?

28:27.300 --> 28:30.840
You can't be a traveler, right?

28:30.980 --> 28:34.760
Yes, that's what I was told.
But of the lowest rank.

28:37.460 --> 28:39.530
Yes!

28:39.660 --> 28:43.850
When I woke up this morning I had a feeling
that something good was going to happen!

28:43.980 --> 28:45.330
You're hurting me.

28:45.460 --> 28:49.730
To us water gods,
travelers are a sign of good luck.

28:49.860 --> 28:54.770
Even my father spent more than
half of his life searching for a traveler

28:54.900 --> 28:58.810
without reward, and yet, I...

28:58.980 --> 29:01.410
Yahoo!

29:01.580 --> 29:05.850
I am Ki-Kima. The first "Ki" is
half a note higher than the "Kima."

29:05.980 --> 29:08.170
If it isn't, it turns into a girl's name!

29:08.300 --> 29:09.650
What's your name?

29:10.380 --> 29:12.890
It's Wataru! Wataru Mitani.

29:13.140 --> 29:15.930
"Wataru." Nice name!

29:27.860 --> 29:31.480
Orca's fin, dried meat of Gimbara,

29:32.220 --> 29:34.490
and the tear of Kiaz-heaven.

29:35.300 --> 29:36.930
All right, you may enter.

29:37.500 --> 29:38.450
Thank you!

29:49.820 --> 29:53.810
- Come in, come in, come in!
- How about this fish?

29:54.020 --> 29:57.330
- It's fresh!
- It's cheap!

29:57.460 --> 30:01.570
- It's very lively.
- Yeah, this is a trade town called Gatara.

30:01.780 --> 30:06.450
Many come here like us, darbada charmers.

30:12.700 --> 30:16.480
Yunababa, save two seats for us!

30:16.620 --> 30:17.600
Okay!

30:19.300 --> 30:20.250
So good.

30:20.580 --> 30:23.040
So that guy who helped the traveler

30:23.180 --> 30:26.330
married Sakawa's number-one beauty
the next month.

30:28.060 --> 30:30.620
Even Dankaron,
who was named King Darbada,

30:30.740 --> 30:33.690
he says it was thanks to eating a meal
with a traveler.

30:34.180 --> 30:38.050
My grandpa only passed by a traveler
outside the town of Tacu,

30:38.180 --> 30:39.570
and he found a mine!

30:39.700 --> 30:43.370
But yeah, it's hard to meet a traveler.

30:47.220 --> 30:49.410
What? You're not eating at all.

30:50.580 --> 30:51.560
Yeah.

30:51.700 --> 30:56.490
This place is a rare store that only opens
when they find good ingredients.

30:56.980 --> 31:00.170
I'll pay for everything so eat till you're full!

31:00.300 --> 31:01.410
Thank you.

31:02.940 --> 31:06.170
So, I need to go deliver the stuff.

31:07.180 --> 31:11.690
If you have leftovers,
Yunababa can get real scary.

31:11.820 --> 31:12.770
Real scary?

31:16.980 --> 31:19.490
Can we pay now, please?

31:19.620 --> 31:20.570
Coming!

31:21.820 --> 31:25.090
I'll be back soon, so no disappearing,

31:25.300 --> 31:27.130
my good-luck giver!

31:36.740 --> 31:39.570
How is it? Is it yummy?

31:40.540 --> 31:42.290
It's really good. Delicious.

31:47.260 --> 31:48.480
Ashikawa!

31:48.980 --> 31:52.810
Hey! Ashikawa! Hey!

31:54.380 --> 31:55.520
Wait! Ashikawa!

31:56.860 --> 31:58.850
Eat it all first!

32:01.820 --> 32:03.130
All right, sit down.

32:06.220 --> 32:08.490
- Thank you!
- Anytime!

32:09.820 --> 32:14.210
Please tell Ki-Kima that I'll be back soon.

32:14.420 --> 32:15.610
Okay!

32:18.940 --> 32:20.130
Which way?

32:22.580 --> 32:23.530
Here we go!

32:34.580 --> 32:37.040
Thank you for waiting,
ladies and gentlemen!

32:37.420 --> 32:41.970
Thank you for coming to see our circus!

32:42.140 --> 32:45.890
Please enjoy

32:46.100 --> 32:49.170
till the very end.

33:11.420 --> 33:12.890
Thank you for waiting.

33:13.020 --> 33:17.770
The first is by the prima donna
of our circus magicians.

33:18.460 --> 33:23.290
Please enjoy Miina's trapeze swing.

33:28.540 --> 33:31.530
What?

34:40.980 --> 34:41.960
What are you doing?

34:48.180 --> 34:50.610
You're wasting my time.

34:53.420 --> 34:56.450
What're you doing?
Close his mouth quickly!

34:56.580 --> 34:57.530
Sorry.

35:00.020 --> 35:02.130
Okay, let's get out of here.

35:02.420 --> 35:04.930
Ashikawa? Sorry, wrong person.

35:06.940 --> 35:09.010
What're you doing?

35:09.220 --> 35:12.330
- Nothing a brat should stick his nose in.
- I'm not going to be turned away with that!

35:12.460 --> 35:13.850
Shut up. Don't come any closer.

35:13.980 --> 35:16.410
- Hey, I told you not to bother us.
- He doesn't like it.

35:16.540 --> 35:17.970
What are you doing?

35:19.900 --> 35:22.650
- Oh, are these people...
- Is someone there?

35:26.860 --> 35:27.810
Who are you?

35:28.660 --> 35:30.130
Wait! I am not suspicious.

35:30.780 --> 35:32.090
What is this?

35:32.500 --> 35:37.250
This is... Wait, what?
The two suspicious guys...

35:37.380 --> 35:38.330
Right?

35:38.540 --> 35:41.970
No, there were no such people.

35:51.020 --> 35:52.530
I brought him, Cutts.

35:54.020 --> 35:56.890
He's the robber who tried
to enter the circus?

35:57.060 --> 35:59.050
No, I'm innocent.

35:59.220 --> 36:01.370
Didn't you try to steal the dragon kid?

36:01.500 --> 36:03.050
It wasn't me!

36:03.340 --> 36:05.970
That's something
we'll have to look at the evidence for.

36:06.660 --> 36:09.090
I just came to this world, and...

36:09.300 --> 36:12.330
This world? Then you must be...

36:12.460 --> 36:16.290
I'm a traveler.
Look, I even have a Brave One's sword.

36:16.780 --> 36:18.530
- So I...
- Quiet!

36:19.020 --> 36:22.800
Whether you're a traveler or an emperor,
a criminal should be punished.

36:26.660 --> 36:29.170
That is the way of us Highlanders.

36:30.460 --> 36:31.730
Please wait!

36:33.580 --> 36:35.810
Please, let me out!

36:39.780 --> 36:41.370
I haven't done anything.

36:44.780 --> 36:46.610
What a relief!

36:47.380 --> 36:51.130
That coward aimed
for when everyone was out.

36:51.260 --> 36:54.450
Terrible! When I find him, I'll beat him up!

36:54.700 --> 36:59.010
- That's impossible.
- What's up, Miina? Are you not happy?

37:00.980 --> 37:02.610
Do I look unhappy?

37:25.100 --> 37:29.570
Can't do it. If it goes on like this,
I really will become guilty.

37:30.580 --> 37:31.530
Wataru?

37:31.820 --> 37:32.770
You are?

37:34.460 --> 37:36.530
I saw you when...

37:41.220 --> 37:42.200
Are you here?

37:43.300 --> 37:46.370
Too bad. You can't see me
no matter where you search.

37:47.020 --> 37:50.930
But I'll show you something better.

37:53.460 --> 37:54.410
This is...

37:59.700 --> 38:00.650
Mum.

38:01.660 --> 38:04.040
I'm sorry, Wataru.

38:11.860 --> 38:13.170
Mum.

38:14.100 --> 38:15.450
I'm sorry.

38:15.780 --> 38:18.810
Who are you? How are you able to do this?

38:20.620 --> 38:22.650
Go to the abandoned church.

38:23.580 --> 38:26.570
Why are you telling me these things?
Why are you helping me?

38:27.060 --> 38:29.010
Because I've taken a liking to you.

38:29.140 --> 38:30.090
Huh?

38:31.300 --> 38:32.250
Bye, Wataru.

38:33.980 --> 38:36.170
Go to the abandoned church, okay?

38:36.540 --> 38:39.000
Wait! I still have questions
I want to ask you!

38:39.220 --> 38:41.050
We'll meet again, Wataru.

38:41.500 --> 38:45.170
So long as you don't give up on your
journey, we will surely meet again.

39:02.700 --> 39:05.130
Hey! Wait, brat!

39:05.340 --> 39:06.850
You're still here?

39:43.460 --> 39:46.410
You really are a traveler to keep an eye on.

39:47.900 --> 39:51.170
Don't misunderstand. You've been set free.

39:51.300 --> 39:52.250
What?

39:53.060 --> 39:55.690
Last night, the dragon kid disappeared.

39:58.820 --> 40:02.130
It would have been impossible for you
who were in jail to have stolen him.

40:02.260 --> 40:03.210
Can you stand?

40:03.420 --> 40:04.370
Yes.

40:05.020 --> 40:06.570
Don't feel relieved just yet.

40:07.180 --> 40:10.690
Until you prove to be innocent
of collaboration, you can't leave this city.

40:12.700 --> 40:13.650
What?

40:14.380 --> 40:17.090
I need to hurry
and collect the five gemstones,

40:17.500 --> 40:19.930
and then ask the Goddess
to save my mother.

40:23.940 --> 40:25.970
I think I know who the suspect is.

40:26.380 --> 40:28.410
- I'll...
- You're gonna do it?

40:29.300 --> 40:32.810
Yes. Please tell me
where the true culprits are.

40:36.340 --> 40:40.450
Wataru, I found you had vanished,
and now you are going there?

40:40.780 --> 40:45.530
Do you know what's under that church?
A cave of no return!

40:45.700 --> 40:48.260
Once you enter the cave,
there's no going back!

40:48.460 --> 40:49.410
We've arrived.

40:50.740 --> 40:54.010
That's their secret hideout.
The abandoned church.

40:56.340 --> 40:59.450
Go to the abandoned church, Wataru.

41:01.300 --> 41:05.130
I'm telling you, it's a bad idea!
There's no going back here!

41:06.380 --> 41:07.600
Huh? It smells like water.

41:08.220 --> 41:11.010
- Water?
- They'll be able to hear you.

41:15.180 --> 41:17.250
Some yummy water is calling me.

41:17.460 --> 41:19.170
Weren't you scared, Ki-Kima?

41:19.300 --> 41:21.530
But the water smells great!

41:24.060 --> 41:27.170
Water! It's the ocean!

41:27.900 --> 41:30.690
Yes! Here we go!

41:31.060 --> 41:34.010
It's been a long time
since I saw a nice pool of water like this.

41:34.140 --> 41:38.570
Water is life for us.
Please excuse me for a moment.

41:38.700 --> 41:40.530
No! You can't!

41:40.660 --> 41:41.640
- Ki-Kima! Wait!
- Don't stop me.

41:41.780 --> 41:43.050
Don't stop me, Wataru!

41:43.180 --> 41:46.450
I guess we should make him
into a stuffed dragon now.

41:46.580 --> 41:48.930
It's dangerous
with him blowing fire everywhere.

41:54.060 --> 41:57.010
Who is it? What do you want?

41:57.300 --> 41:59.330
You shouldn't come to places like this.

41:59.740 --> 42:04.370
Who's the leader here?
Return the dragon kid!

42:04.660 --> 42:07.330
Dragon? Don't know anything about it.

42:07.460 --> 42:08.410
Liar!

42:09.300 --> 42:11.860
You said you were only going to
keep him as a pet!

42:12.140 --> 42:13.650
You're going to betray us?

42:13.780 --> 42:17.130
It was a lie that you would bring me
to my father, too, wasn't it?

42:17.620 --> 42:19.050
- This is bad!
- Wait!

42:19.380 --> 42:20.810
Let her go!

42:31.180 --> 42:33.210
Bright! It's too bright!

42:35.140 --> 42:36.090
Wataru!

42:43.980 --> 42:47.010
Hang on, Wataru!

43:21.660 --> 43:23.090
That was something.

43:23.220 --> 43:25.680
Don't have it. Don't have it!
I don't have my sword!

43:25.860 --> 43:27.530
I need to go look for it!

43:27.660 --> 43:28.970
Wataru! Hey!

43:29.300 --> 43:31.250
You're going to go back again?

43:48.300 --> 43:49.730
Wataru!

44:01.060 --> 44:03.090
Why?

44:21.220 --> 44:23.330
Impressive, Wataru!

44:44.220 --> 44:46.890
Wataru, are you alive? Are you still alive?

44:49.620 --> 44:51.250
Wataru!

45:02.340 --> 45:04.050
You okay, Wataru?

45:04.300 --> 45:05.250
I guess.

45:06.740 --> 45:11.410
I wonder if this is thanks to that voice.

45:12.420 --> 45:14.210
Seeing those monsters,

45:15.020 --> 45:20.610
even the Highlanders ran home
as fast as they could. Were you not scared?

45:21.380 --> 45:25.080
It was terrifying!
I really thought they'd eat me!

45:26.180 --> 45:28.010
I like you, traveler.

45:28.780 --> 45:30.130
Toron, the preparations.

45:30.300 --> 45:31.250
Yes.

45:44.460 --> 45:45.410
This is?

45:45.620 --> 45:47.890
It's us Highlanders' badge.

45:48.340 --> 45:50.770
Only those who bring about justice
can wear it.

45:51.340 --> 45:52.290
Justice...

45:53.340 --> 45:57.730
By wearing this, it will probably
help in your quest for gemstones.

45:58.220 --> 46:02.850
But at the same time, you must take
responsibility as a Highlander.

46:03.020 --> 46:05.090
You mean by bringing about justice?

46:05.260 --> 46:09.170
Yes! Whether your opponent is strong
or you incur loss.

46:10.780 --> 46:11.730
Can you do it?

46:13.420 --> 46:17.890
I'll try hard not to betray your trust.

46:18.300 --> 46:19.250
All right.

46:19.740 --> 46:21.770
Then you will vow on the bracelet.

46:22.100 --> 46:23.050
How?

46:23.460 --> 46:25.610
Put the bracelet on your left wrist.

46:28.820 --> 46:30.490
It's a bit big.

46:31.300 --> 46:34.840
Tap my bracelet with yours twice.

46:35.540 --> 46:36.490
Yes.

46:40.780 --> 46:44.770
Congratulations!
With this, you, too, are a Highlander.

46:45.260 --> 46:46.210
Yes!

46:56.620 --> 46:58.610
Come here!

46:59.820 --> 47:03.930
Didn't Cutts say that she would depend
on you to watch over the new Highlander?

47:05.580 --> 47:08.090
See? This guy ended up coming along, too.

47:08.220 --> 47:09.170
But...

47:09.340 --> 47:10.290
It's okay!

47:11.700 --> 47:12.650
Yeah!

47:15.100 --> 47:16.730
I'm Wataru. You?

47:16.980 --> 47:21.330
Miina. That kid is Fire Dragon's child, Jozo.

47:25.860 --> 47:28.370
Wataru is our good-luck giver!

47:28.500 --> 47:32.040
By traveling with him,
I'm sure you'll find your father.

49:14.180 --> 49:15.970
Have one, too, Wataru.

49:18.260 --> 49:21.090
Wataru? Wataru!

49:23.500 --> 49:24.610
Miina!

49:25.540 --> 49:26.490
Ki-Kima!

49:36.380 --> 49:40.850
Were you separated from your companions,
young Highlander?

49:41.420 --> 49:42.450
Huh?

49:42.580 --> 49:44.730
You are having some trouble, I reckon.

49:44.860 --> 49:48.170
Let me have my men look for them.

49:48.300 --> 49:49.250
You are?

49:49.820 --> 49:54.810
I am he who governs Giris, Bishop Daimon.

50:17.260 --> 50:20.250
I am sorry for putting you through
so much trouble.

50:20.820 --> 50:25.610
What are you saying?
You haven't touched a thing.

50:26.140 --> 50:27.530
There's no reason to hold back.

50:27.740 --> 50:29.890
Thanks to you Highlanders,

50:30.020 --> 50:33.250
my country is able to live in peace.

50:33.620 --> 50:34.570
Thank you.

50:35.620 --> 50:37.090
For dessert,

50:37.220 --> 50:41.810
I thought I would have Bauwauwa prepared,

50:42.020 --> 50:45.530
but there was a terrible forest fire in Makiba.

50:46.060 --> 50:50.050
All the Bauwauwa trees were burnt,
without a single one remaining.

50:50.780 --> 50:54.890
A traveler, in search of gemstones,
burnt down the forest.

50:55.020 --> 50:55.970
What?

50:56.100 --> 50:59.930
To be able to burn the entire forest
is scary magic, indeed.

51:00.420 --> 51:03.810
By the reports, the person responsible was
still a child, and one with a pretty face.

51:03.940 --> 51:04.890
It's Ashikawa.

51:05.260 --> 51:07.640
Please give me the details of that story!

51:08.020 --> 51:10.450
Why don't I show you around
Torianka Hospital?

51:10.820 --> 51:14.410
Many of those injured from the forest fire
have been admitted there.

51:14.540 --> 51:17.570
It would be better for you
to hear it straight from them.

51:17.700 --> 51:21.480
Thank you very much.
May my companions come with me?

51:22.940 --> 51:24.370
No problem.

51:24.500 --> 51:28.120
I will arrange for them to catch up with you
almost immediately.

51:32.620 --> 51:36.490
Release us from here, Wataru!

52:00.740 --> 52:05.210
Even though there were many people
in these woods,

52:05.740 --> 52:10.570
the magician burnt down the woods
without any hesitation.

52:12.620 --> 52:15.610
Because of what he did,
nearly 40 lives were lost.

52:16.500 --> 52:17.970
That's terrible.

52:18.780 --> 52:23.250
Besides doing that,
the magician destroyed a castle

52:23.860 --> 52:26.090
and flooded a river.

52:27.460 --> 52:29.250
- Ashikawa would...
- What?

52:29.380 --> 52:31.570
Ashikawa wouldn't do something like that!

52:32.220 --> 52:34.450
It's probably some sort of mistake.

52:34.740 --> 52:35.690
Wataru!

52:37.020 --> 52:38.530
Can you hear my voice?

52:42.780 --> 52:45.610
- Who are you?
- You cannot enter that building. It's a trap.

52:45.740 --> 52:47.050
What's wrong?

52:48.220 --> 52:52.570
That man is an enemy. Trust in me, Wataru.

52:55.700 --> 52:57.450
Excuse me.

52:57.580 --> 52:59.610
I just remembered an important thing
I need to do.

52:59.900 --> 53:02.650
That's it. Quickly, run away from here!

53:02.780 --> 53:03.890
I understand.

53:05.340 --> 53:06.730
If that's the way it is.

53:08.420 --> 53:11.530
Actually, he's in this hospital.

53:12.340 --> 53:14.170
The magician who started the forest fire.

53:14.340 --> 53:15.290
What?

53:16.100 --> 53:18.450
He has severe burns on his body.

53:18.940 --> 53:22.130
The doctor says that his life is in danger.

53:22.260 --> 53:23.930
- That's why...
- Ashikawa!

53:33.060 --> 53:35.810
Wataru!
You can't just go in there by yourself!

53:36.220 --> 53:39.410
Where is he, the magician who got burnt?

53:40.180 --> 53:43.720
If it's he you're looking for,
he's over there. Look!

53:49.300 --> 53:50.360
Dad!

53:50.620 --> 53:53.610
What's wrong, Wataru?

53:54.780 --> 53:58.250
Mum collapsed!
Please, go to the hospital for her!

54:00.180 --> 54:04.370
I'm not returning home any more.
I already said that.

54:05.580 --> 54:10.440
Dad, did you come to dislike Mum and me?

54:11.340 --> 54:12.290
No.

54:13.420 --> 54:16.370
When you become an adult,
you'll understand, too.

54:18.340 --> 54:21.610
Then I'm fine with remaining as a child.

54:22.580 --> 54:24.490
Hurting children...

54:25.420 --> 54:29.410
I don't want to become
like that sort of adult!

54:29.620 --> 54:32.810
- I'd much rather choose to remain as a...
- Shut up!

54:33.460 --> 54:38.650
You don't know how much
I've been putting up with all this time.

54:39.060 --> 54:41.210
Don't talk about things
you know nothing about!

54:41.340 --> 54:44.330
I worked and worked, and I even worked
through some of my sleeping hours.

54:44.460 --> 54:47.050
Many times I held back
from getting a new car I wanted.

54:47.620 --> 54:51.610
But with all that, no one was kind to me.
No one was grateful.

54:51.940 --> 54:53.810
They take it for granted!

54:54.940 --> 54:57.170
Is that how I'm supposed to live my life?

54:57.340 --> 55:00.290
What if I want to eat good food,
and buy what I want?

55:00.420 --> 55:05.130
Can't I live for myself? For just myself?

55:06.460 --> 55:09.020
I hate it!

55:09.740 --> 55:12.450
So that's why, my position as an adult,

55:14.100 --> 55:18.330
as a husband, and as a father,
I refuse them all!

55:41.460 --> 55:42.730
Break!

55:56.660 --> 55:57.610
Dad!

55:58.180 --> 55:59.490
You mean those leaves are him?

56:01.420 --> 56:05.690
You've got a strange father, huh?
Huh, Mitani!

56:06.740 --> 56:08.050
Ashikawa!

56:09.180 --> 56:12.410
Do you think I would get burnt
from my own magic?

56:15.340 --> 56:18.410
For now, I've repaid my debts.

56:22.420 --> 56:23.690
Who's in there?

56:33.260 --> 56:36.530
Were you the one who wrote the spell
on the roof?

56:36.740 --> 56:41.600
Who do you think you're talking to?

56:41.820 --> 56:46.450
I don't know what you were trying to do
when you wrote that, but it was wrong.

56:46.980 --> 56:50.170
The direction was off,
and the length of the line was wrong.

56:50.740 --> 56:52.410
Who'd you learn magic from?

56:52.820 --> 56:54.210
Did you actually graduate?

56:54.340 --> 56:56.490
Are you going to insult me?

56:56.620 --> 56:58.920
I'm just asking you some questions.

56:59.740 --> 57:01.770
It's kind of hard to hear you
from so far away.

57:02.060 --> 57:05.210
Would you mind coming up here?

57:05.700 --> 57:08.130
Isn't it easy by using Air Ladder magic?

57:10.100 --> 57:13.170
Oh. You can't even use Air Ladder?

57:34.540 --> 57:38.690
My faithful servant, strike down the evil one!

57:43.060 --> 57:46.930
Receive an arrow from my spirit!

58:09.700 --> 58:12.410
Stop, Ashikawa! He'll die!

58:13.700 --> 58:16.160
He's the guy who tried to kill you,
you know.

58:16.820 --> 58:19.770
And plus, you heard, didn't you?

58:20.660 --> 58:23.850
What I've done to get the gemstones
into my hand.

58:26.020 --> 58:30.770
But you had a reason, right? Tell me!

58:32.940 --> 58:35.610
I want to believe you!

58:37.300 --> 58:40.250
You didn't think that many animals
were going to die.

58:40.380 --> 58:45.370
You didn't realize so many people
would get hurt.

58:45.500 --> 58:46.450
Stop!

58:46.940 --> 58:50.370
Mitani! Why did you come to Vision?

58:51.300 --> 58:55.000
Did you come here to make friends
in Vision?

58:56.100 --> 58:59.050
Did you come here to preserve peace
in Vision?

59:03.380 --> 59:06.650
I came here because of my mum.

59:09.980 --> 59:14.250
I came here
to find the last of the gemstones.

59:16.380 --> 59:18.050
I'm going to Irda Empire.

59:20.100 --> 59:25.090
To get my wish granted,
I would do anything.

59:45.700 --> 59:46.760
Come on!

59:47.940 --> 59:50.850
It's okay! I dropped it!

59:52.060 --> 59:55.170
No, this is... My tongue got twisted.

01:00:12.500 --> 01:00:16.250
You're worrying for me? It's okay, Jozo.

01:00:16.900 --> 01:00:21.730
Instead of that, right now,
we have to save Ki-Kima and Miina!

01:00:56.340 --> 01:00:57.320
What's this?

01:01:05.900 --> 01:01:09.050
You've returned alive
from that magic hospital,

01:01:09.380 --> 01:01:13.570
as may be expected from someone who
became a Highlander at such a young age.

01:01:13.700 --> 01:01:15.570
Return Ki-Kima and Miina!

01:01:18.340 --> 01:01:22.490
If you become one of us,
I can let you see them.

01:01:24.140 --> 01:01:25.330
What?

01:01:27.940 --> 01:01:29.000
Who is it?

01:01:30.780 --> 01:01:31.810
Highlanders!

01:01:32.420 --> 01:01:33.730
Cutts!

01:01:35.980 --> 01:01:38.440
Wataru! Over here, over here!

01:01:38.620 --> 01:01:40.290
Ki-Kima! Miina!

01:01:40.460 --> 01:01:44.210
Don't let anyone escape! Catch them
and accomplish the plan of the empire.

01:02:00.020 --> 01:02:02.010
We're not going to let you escape.

01:02:02.140 --> 01:02:03.250
You!

01:02:12.020 --> 01:02:12.970
Magic, huh?

01:02:14.740 --> 01:02:17.410
Don't block my way.

01:02:17.540 --> 01:02:18.490
Wait!

01:02:29.340 --> 01:02:30.730
It's dangerous! That stick...

01:02:53.420 --> 01:02:54.400
You okay, Wataru?

01:02:54.540 --> 01:02:55.490
Cutts.

01:02:56.260 --> 01:02:57.210
Here.

01:03:02.940 --> 01:03:05.450
This has turned into a major problem.

01:03:05.700 --> 01:03:06.650
What's wrong?

01:03:08.300 --> 01:03:11.650
Irda Empire joined forces
with a powerful magician.

01:03:11.780 --> 01:03:12.730
What?

01:03:12.860 --> 01:03:17.130
A force supported by the magician's power
is heading towards us.

01:03:18.180 --> 01:03:20.050
At this rate, we will have a war.

01:03:32.100 --> 01:03:36.490
Irda Empire.
That's where Ashikawa said he would go.

01:03:39.340 --> 01:03:43.890
Then the powerful magician is Ashikawa?

01:04:00.260 --> 01:04:03.050
Do you dislike dances, Princess Zofie?

01:04:04.420 --> 01:04:05.770
Mr Magician.

01:04:06.540 --> 01:04:08.090
Please call me Mitsuru.

01:04:09.020 --> 01:04:10.650
Mitsuru.

01:04:11.380 --> 01:04:12.570
If it is okay with you,

01:04:13.780 --> 01:04:16.890
would you care to teach me how to dance?

01:04:23.580 --> 01:04:24.610
Like this?

01:04:31.100 --> 01:04:32.810
Where have you come from?

01:04:34.260 --> 01:04:36.090
A place you wouldn't know.

01:04:37.180 --> 01:04:40.530
From the South? Or maybe the East?

01:04:41.460 --> 01:04:43.810
"Between the moon and the stars."

01:04:44.420 --> 01:04:46.650
Would that be an acceptable answer?

01:04:46.780 --> 01:04:49.370
Is that where your family is?

01:04:53.860 --> 01:04:55.610
My younger sister is.

01:04:59.100 --> 01:05:01.010
What about your friends?

01:05:04.220 --> 01:05:07.010
If I may count a strange one, I have one.

01:05:11.860 --> 01:05:16.770
Judging from your expression,
he or she must be a very precious friend.

01:05:21.460 --> 01:05:25.930
Do you know about a gemstone
with the power of darkness?

01:05:26.420 --> 01:05:27.370
What?

01:05:28.460 --> 01:05:32.930
I would like to see it once.
I heard that it is somewhere in this country.

01:05:35.180 --> 01:05:36.130
I'm sorry.

01:05:38.300 --> 01:05:42.290
If what I asked is impossible to do,
I'm sorry.

01:05:43.500 --> 01:05:45.410
Please forget about it.

01:05:51.460 --> 01:05:57.050
This castle was built to protect the gem
with the power of darkness.

01:05:57.540 --> 01:05:59.450
- To protect?
- Yes.

01:06:00.180 --> 01:06:04.770
The gemstone of darkness
suppresses the monsters in this place.

01:06:05.980 --> 01:06:10.690
If the gemstone of darkness is taken,
it is said that monsters would come out,

01:06:11.260 --> 01:06:13.850
and Vision would be destroyed.

01:06:14.860 --> 01:06:17.210
So unless you destroy the castle...

01:06:18.180 --> 01:06:21.570
Yes, you cannot go near
the gemstone of darkness.

01:06:22.100 --> 01:06:27.650
And even if you destroy the castle,
by the gemstone lies a mirror

01:06:27.780 --> 01:06:31.290
which would reflect
that person's biggest terror.

01:06:33.620 --> 01:06:37.770
Do you feel ready to face that mirror?

01:06:42.340 --> 01:06:43.290
You know.

01:06:45.020 --> 01:06:46.810
If I were to look into that mirror,

01:06:47.940 --> 01:06:51.290
probably you would be reflected in it.

01:07:15.940 --> 01:07:17.730
Jozo, what's wrong?

01:07:25.260 --> 01:07:27.930
Would we be allowed to do anything

01:07:29.820 --> 01:07:31.770
if it's for the sake of a precious wish?

01:07:33.540 --> 01:07:35.010
Wataru!

01:07:35.340 --> 01:07:37.970
It's cold.
I brought something warm for you.

01:07:39.220 --> 01:07:41.250
Thank you. What about you?

01:07:41.380 --> 01:07:43.410
I'm fine. I'm from the cat family!

01:07:49.140 --> 01:07:50.090
There you go.

01:07:52.500 --> 01:07:54.010
It's very warm, isn't it?

01:07:56.340 --> 01:07:57.290
Yeah.

01:08:00.540 --> 01:08:05.850
What wish are you going to ask
the Goddess of Destiny to grant?

01:08:06.180 --> 01:08:07.130
Huh?

01:08:07.580 --> 01:08:12.050
I heard that travelers from other worlds
come to do that.

01:08:16.220 --> 01:08:20.090
I came to get my family back.

01:08:22.500 --> 01:08:25.370
My father left home,

01:08:26.300 --> 01:08:30.850
and my mum collapsed. So...

01:08:33.300 --> 01:08:36.920
I see. It's the same as me.

01:08:37.100 --> 01:08:38.050
What?

01:08:41.700 --> 01:08:45.290
My mum died when I was little,

01:08:46.580 --> 01:08:50.850
so I only had a father.

01:08:52.060 --> 01:08:53.490
So that's why you did that?

01:08:56.020 --> 01:08:59.530
But, when I look back on it now,
I know it was wrong.

01:09:00.860 --> 01:09:02.650
I want to meet my father,

01:09:02.820 --> 01:09:06.210
but it's not like you can make excuses for
doing something that's wrong, right?

01:09:08.060 --> 01:09:09.810
Sorry, Jozo.

01:09:12.180 --> 01:09:15.720
That's why I think you're something.

01:09:16.260 --> 01:09:17.210
Me?

01:09:17.700 --> 01:09:18.650
Yeah.

01:09:19.020 --> 01:09:22.560
Because, unlike that other traveler,

01:09:23.140 --> 01:09:25.130
you don't do bad stuff, right?

01:09:26.340 --> 01:09:28.930
No matter how much of a great magician
he might be...

01:09:29.660 --> 01:09:32.250
I don't like that.

01:09:35.820 --> 01:09:38.410
Sorry! He's one of your friends, right?

01:09:39.540 --> 01:09:42.210
No, it's okay.

01:09:43.580 --> 01:09:48.440
Because it is true that Ashikawa
has done wrong to the people in this world.

01:09:49.900 --> 01:09:53.410
But Ashikawa,

01:09:54.580 --> 01:09:59.210
if you are going to such great lengths
to change it,

01:10:00.700 --> 01:10:03.650
what type of destiny
are you trying to change?

01:10:05.500 --> 01:10:06.450
What?

01:10:12.900 --> 01:10:13.850
Is this a horn?

01:10:14.020 --> 01:10:17.410
Congratulations!
I hope you'll have a nice horn.

01:10:17.540 --> 01:10:20.100
Huh? I didn't know that dragons
re-grow their horns.

01:10:22.780 --> 01:10:25.730
- He said to blow into it.
- Blow into it?

01:10:26.340 --> 01:10:27.290
Like this?

01:10:38.900 --> 01:10:41.010
There's not really much sound coming out.

01:11:06.740 --> 01:11:10.330
It's cold, isn't it? Cold!

01:11:11.980 --> 01:11:14.010
I didn't know he was Jozo's father.

01:11:14.820 --> 01:11:18.050
We will occupy Emperor Irda's castle,
Crystal Palace.

01:11:18.180 --> 01:11:21.490
Yes! We're going to stop the war, right?

01:11:21.620 --> 01:11:24.050
Yes. As Highlanders.

01:11:24.580 --> 01:11:25.560
Look!

01:11:26.660 --> 01:11:29.040
What are those?

01:11:29.180 --> 01:11:31.090
It's the Empire's main fleet.

01:11:32.860 --> 01:11:35.210
That's a terrifying number!

01:11:35.500 --> 01:11:38.370
So many ships.

01:11:38.820 --> 01:11:41.250
This is bad.
The speed of the ships is too fast.

01:11:41.460 --> 01:11:43.530
First we will arrest the Emperor.

01:11:48.660 --> 01:11:50.530
Wataru? Wataru?

01:11:50.780 --> 01:11:54.370
Mitsuru has found out how to get
to the gem of darkness. Hurry!

01:11:55.020 --> 01:11:56.050
Ashikawa has?

01:11:56.180 --> 01:11:59.610
Yes. Mitsuru is going to
bring Vision to ruin!

01:12:53.340 --> 01:12:55.410
Wataru! Irda Empire!

01:13:29.620 --> 01:13:31.450
Princess Zofie, please go back.

01:13:32.980 --> 01:13:34.330
Mitsuru.

01:13:42.660 --> 01:13:43.930
Ashikawa!

01:13:44.860 --> 01:13:46.130
Ashikawa!

01:14:15.660 --> 01:14:19.010
Stop! You cannot go any further.

01:14:19.260 --> 01:14:20.210
Get out of my way.

01:14:20.380 --> 01:14:22.970
Mitsuru! Why?

01:15:17.740 --> 01:15:20.930
This is where the last gemstone is.

01:15:59.940 --> 01:16:02.570
This is the gem of darkness.

01:16:23.380 --> 01:16:24.410
Wataru!

01:16:24.540 --> 01:16:26.410
Forget about the Emperor.
Follow the magician!

01:16:26.540 --> 01:16:27.570
Yes.

01:16:27.700 --> 01:16:29.090
Wataru!

01:16:33.060 --> 01:16:35.250
Wait for me, Aya.

01:16:35.700 --> 01:16:39.370
Mitsuru, please! Don't take the gemstone!

01:16:40.420 --> 01:16:41.370
Mitsuru!

01:16:42.220 --> 01:16:45.010
I am a traveler, Princess.

01:16:47.260 --> 01:16:51.730
If I can just get the gem of darkness,
the path to the Tower of Fortune will open.

01:16:52.780 --> 01:16:54.850
Please don't.

01:16:58.660 --> 01:17:02.090
Ashikawa! Stop, Ashikawa!

01:17:02.860 --> 01:17:05.530
Mitani, this has nothing to do with you!

01:17:07.180 --> 01:17:08.160
Don't come!

01:17:16.780 --> 01:17:20.290
Ashikawa! You care nothing about
what will happen to Vision?

01:17:20.500 --> 01:17:24.970
I don't care what happens to Vision.
I have something more important to me.

01:17:25.220 --> 01:17:26.810
Mitani, even you do.

01:17:31.660 --> 01:17:33.890
I thought like you, Ashikawa.

01:17:34.700 --> 01:17:37.970
But I think you're wrong.

01:17:38.140 --> 01:17:41.090
I don't care if I am wrong,
as long as I can change my destiny!

01:17:42.060 --> 01:17:44.410
And you'll be happy with that?

01:17:44.900 --> 01:17:48.490
If I don't get my wish fulfilled,
then there was no point in coming to Vision!

01:17:48.620 --> 01:17:49.760
You idiot!

01:17:50.220 --> 01:17:52.680
Shut up, you sissy!

01:17:57.940 --> 01:18:02.250
Ashikawa! I don't want to fight you!

01:18:02.380 --> 01:18:06.410
Shut up!
You've had an easy life so you can say that!

01:18:15.340 --> 01:18:16.610
Wataru!

01:18:18.100 --> 01:18:19.890
Wataru is fine.

01:18:25.740 --> 01:18:28.610
Let's stop now.
This isn't like you, Ashikawa.

01:18:28.780 --> 01:18:30.090
What is like me?

01:18:30.540 --> 01:18:35.130
What do you think you know about me?

01:18:35.740 --> 01:18:37.890
A heartbreaking report on a family suicide.

01:18:38.020 --> 01:18:38.970
Family suicide!

01:18:39.100 --> 01:18:42.090
Those who died were Mitsuaki Ashikawa, 35,

01:18:42.220 --> 01:18:46.050
and his family.
According to the police investigation...

01:18:46.300 --> 01:18:50.530
Mitsuaki murdered his wife, Aki, 29,

01:18:50.660 --> 01:18:54.330
and Aki's male acquaintance,
and committed suicide,

01:18:54.460 --> 01:18:58.160
- killing their daughter Aya, age 2, with them.
- Stop! Don't show this to me!

01:19:13.300 --> 01:19:16.370
Ashikawa. That's why you want
to change your destiny.

01:19:17.020 --> 01:19:19.130
Stop! Stop!

01:19:21.460 --> 01:19:23.290
Ashikawa!

01:19:23.420 --> 01:19:27.690
Open up, Ashikawa! Hey, Ashikawa!

01:19:27.820 --> 01:19:31.850
I didn't know that that sort of thing
had happened. I'm sorry!

01:19:32.100 --> 01:19:34.970
I'm sorry, Ashikawa. Ashikawa!

01:19:35.580 --> 01:19:38.730
Ashikawa! I'm sorry, Ashikawa!

01:19:58.260 --> 01:19:59.650
Bye-bye!

01:20:00.060 --> 01:20:01.650
- Come back soon, okay?
- Got it!

01:20:01.820 --> 01:20:05.410
- Come on!
- That's it, that's it! Over here!

01:20:05.980 --> 01:20:09.170
- Over here!
- Come on!

01:20:09.380 --> 01:20:11.840
- Yes!
- Yes!

01:20:11.980 --> 01:20:12.930
We did it!

01:20:24.460 --> 01:20:27.890
Aya, I'll raise you back now.

01:20:31.900 --> 01:20:36.840
This type of destiny...

01:20:37.540 --> 01:20:39.210
I'll change it!

01:20:40.460 --> 01:20:43.530
Ashikawa! Ashikawa!

01:22:02.300 --> 01:22:05.690
He got hold of the gemstone.

01:22:16.300 --> 01:22:17.490
Are you okay?

01:22:18.900 --> 01:22:20.250
Please...

01:22:22.180 --> 01:22:24.690
Please stop Mitsuru.

01:22:26.020 --> 01:22:28.850
I am planning on doing so. Are you okay?

01:22:35.180 --> 01:22:36.770
Please take this.

01:22:43.820 --> 01:22:45.450
Take care of this.

01:22:46.260 --> 01:22:47.210
Wataru!

01:22:53.060 --> 01:22:55.010
Are you going to the Tower of Fortune?

01:22:55.700 --> 01:22:56.650
Yes.

01:22:58.060 --> 01:23:00.010
I need to once more

01:23:00.780 --> 01:23:04.090
meet with Ashikawa.

01:23:05.700 --> 01:23:10.010
All right, then, Wataru. Go.
We'll take care of the monsters.

01:23:11.060 --> 01:23:12.010
Yes.

01:23:18.220 --> 01:23:20.330
Wataru, have a safe trip.

01:23:22.620 --> 01:23:23.570
Miina!

01:24:07.780 --> 01:24:08.810
This is the end!

01:24:09.140 --> 01:24:10.730
You okay?

01:24:11.580 --> 01:24:12.530
Yes.

01:24:16.060 --> 01:24:17.690
It will not do to give up.

01:24:18.020 --> 01:24:19.770
- Ms Zofie!
- Princess!

01:24:19.900 --> 01:24:20.880
Your Highness!

01:24:21.180 --> 01:24:24.210
We are still living.

01:24:24.820 --> 01:24:28.330
And while we are still living,
it will not do to lose hope.

01:25:00.060 --> 01:25:04.690
Vision is in a terrible state! Ashikawa!

01:25:06.900 --> 01:25:08.040
A Brave One's sword?

01:25:12.420 --> 01:25:14.130
Is that me?

01:25:25.940 --> 01:25:28.850
Why? No matter how you look at it,
that is me.

01:25:45.260 --> 01:25:49.730
Better hurry, or Ashikawa will get his wish
fulfilled before you. Are you okay with that?

01:25:52.780 --> 01:25:54.090
I missed!

01:26:01.860 --> 01:26:03.250
I'm so sorry, Cutts.

01:26:03.380 --> 01:26:04.330
You owe me something.

01:26:04.580 --> 01:26:05.530
Yes.

01:26:06.460 --> 01:26:07.520
Cutts!

01:26:17.180 --> 01:26:21.570
Don't just go kissing me
before asking me out.

01:26:21.860 --> 01:26:23.130
You bastard.

01:26:24.500 --> 01:26:28.490
Oh, yeah! I just need to defeat Ashikawa
and then take the gemstone from him.

01:26:28.980 --> 01:26:31.770
Wow! That's a brilliant idea!

01:26:34.860 --> 01:26:37.240
Stop! If I don't hurry, Vision will...

01:26:37.380 --> 01:26:41.250
Liar! You really don't care
about what happens to Vision.

01:26:41.380 --> 01:26:42.930
That's not true!

01:26:43.220 --> 01:26:47.210
Liar! I am you! That's how I know!

01:27:03.620 --> 01:27:06.410
You don't care about anyone but yourself.

01:27:07.860 --> 01:27:09.610
That's not true!

01:27:09.740 --> 01:27:12.330
No, Wataru! You cannot hurt him.

01:27:12.460 --> 01:27:15.610
- He is nobody but you.
- I came to change my destiny!

01:27:15.780 --> 01:27:18.930
And I didn't care about anything else.
Am I wrong?

01:27:19.460 --> 01:27:22.410
That may be true, but...

01:27:40.100 --> 01:27:41.050
Aya!

01:28:03.620 --> 01:28:06.410
Father, wait! Don't leave!

01:28:07.620 --> 01:28:08.930
Come back!

01:28:09.940 --> 01:28:13.250
Mum! Wake up! Don't leave me alone!

01:28:14.220 --> 01:28:17.530
Shut up, you sissy!

01:28:17.660 --> 01:28:21.530
Liar! You really don't care
about what happens to Vision.

01:28:22.060 --> 01:28:26.650
Oh, yeah.
That time, I thought I could do anything

01:28:26.940 --> 01:28:30.330
to change my destiny
or for the sake of my mum.

01:28:31.140 --> 01:28:33.330
If only I could just change my destiny.

01:28:33.460 --> 01:28:37.080
But not if I end up saying,
"I don't care what happens to Vision!"

01:28:37.220 --> 01:28:42.340
Not like that. Because Mum...

01:28:49.780 --> 01:28:54.170
Being sad, getting mad, wanting love,
holding grudges against people

01:28:55.540 --> 01:29:00.330
and blaming others, they're all a part of me.

01:29:02.100 --> 01:29:05.690
That's right. You are me.

01:29:06.980 --> 01:29:10.410
But there are other things that we can do.

01:29:14.340 --> 01:29:15.450
Welcome back.

01:30:08.500 --> 01:30:09.610
Ashikawa!

01:30:10.900 --> 01:30:13.890
No! That is your...

01:30:15.940 --> 01:30:17.730
Mitsuru!

01:30:30.500 --> 01:30:31.640
Mitsuru!

01:30:33.100 --> 01:30:34.050
Mitsuru!

01:30:35.420 --> 01:30:38.450
Mitani, why do you care about me?

01:30:39.140 --> 01:30:40.650
Because we're friends.

01:30:41.300 --> 01:30:43.930
You really are a hypocrite.

01:30:45.780 --> 01:30:46.730
Wataru.

01:30:48.180 --> 01:30:49.130
Mitsuru.

01:30:49.980 --> 01:30:53.170
I wonder when it started going wrong.

01:30:54.340 --> 01:30:55.290
I'm sorry.

01:30:57.220 --> 01:31:00.650
Why are you apologizing?

01:31:01.500 --> 01:31:02.450
Because...

01:31:03.620 --> 01:31:06.650
Wataru, you won.

01:31:07.780 --> 01:31:10.730
Rejoice.

01:31:11.980 --> 01:31:15.730
Why are you crying?

01:31:16.220 --> 01:31:19.050
To the very end,

01:31:21.260 --> 01:31:24.250
you really are a hypocrite, huh?

01:31:26.100 --> 01:31:29.170
Don't say "the end"! We'll go home together!

01:31:29.820 --> 01:31:33.520
We'll return home, go to school,
play soccer and games.

01:31:33.780 --> 01:31:35.290
And we'll go to middle school.

01:31:35.820 --> 01:31:39.690
I lost. I will die here.

01:31:40.340 --> 01:31:43.250
I couldn't change my destiny.

01:31:46.740 --> 01:31:47.690
Mitsuru!

01:31:48.380 --> 01:31:52.650
Go! Leave me.

01:31:52.820 --> 01:31:57.050
No! I don't want to go
and leave you here alone.

01:31:57.620 --> 01:32:00.210
You idiot! You're not in your right mind.

01:32:07.420 --> 01:32:11.690
I'm fine by myself.

01:32:12.660 --> 01:32:16.130
Shut up! I will definitely bring you back.

01:32:16.380 --> 01:32:18.570
Whatever I do, I will bring you back.

01:32:19.100 --> 01:32:21.330
Mitsuru! Mitsuru!

01:32:26.740 --> 01:32:31.450
Is that you, Aya? I see.

01:32:32.860 --> 01:32:34.000
Finally.

01:32:38.700 --> 01:32:41.810
Big brother, here's a present for you!

01:32:45.340 --> 01:32:48.370
Happy Birthday to you

01:33:11.700 --> 01:33:15.650
Welcome home, big brother!

01:33:18.060 --> 01:33:19.280
I'm back!

01:33:30.740 --> 01:33:32.650
Mitsuru? Mitsuru!

01:33:35.620 --> 01:33:37.650
Don't go! Mitsuru!

01:33:38.260 --> 01:33:39.650
Hey, Mitsuru!

01:33:44.140 --> 01:33:45.930
Mitsuru!

01:34:12.340 --> 01:34:14.010
Poor Wataru.

01:34:15.420 --> 01:34:18.490
The Goddess of Destiny really does
terrible things.

01:34:19.220 --> 01:34:21.410
She divided two best friends.

01:34:21.860 --> 01:34:23.050
That voice is

01:34:23.420 --> 01:34:25.650
the voice that always rescued me.

01:34:25.900 --> 01:34:29.130
Your remembered me? I'm so happy!

01:34:33.940 --> 01:34:36.650
Hey, Wataru.
Do you want to rescue Mitsuru?

01:34:36.780 --> 01:34:37.730
Huh?

01:34:37.860 --> 01:34:41.610
And the big man from the water-god family
and the girl from the cat family?

01:34:42.820 --> 01:34:45.050
And your father and mother?

01:34:46.220 --> 01:34:48.090
You want to change your destiny, right?

01:34:48.380 --> 01:34:50.610
Yes, but...

01:34:51.820 --> 01:34:55.520
You can only have one wish fulfilled.

01:34:56.420 --> 01:34:59.770
But there is a way to grant all your wishes.

01:35:03.700 --> 01:35:05.490
If the Goddess disappeared,

01:35:05.860 --> 01:35:09.560
and you became the God of Vision,

01:35:09.940 --> 01:35:12.530
then, if you like,

01:35:12.780 --> 01:35:16.810
you can grant as many wishes as you want,
whatever they may be.

01:35:18.700 --> 01:35:23.010
Wish it!
Something like "Goddess, be destroyed!"

01:35:33.900 --> 01:35:36.170
Miina! Miina!

01:35:36.340 --> 01:35:38.570
Father!

01:35:39.860 --> 01:35:40.840
Father!

01:35:40.980 --> 01:35:42.610
- Miina!
- What's wrong, Miina? Miina!

01:35:45.140 --> 01:35:46.650
Miina! Miina!

01:35:49.780 --> 01:35:50.730
Miina!

01:35:51.420 --> 01:35:53.330
- Father!
- Miina!

01:35:53.460 --> 01:35:55.010
Father, run away!

01:36:00.500 --> 01:36:03.810
- Papa! Papa!
- It's all right now. It's all right now, Miina.

01:36:04.660 --> 01:36:08.010
Miina! Miina!

01:36:08.140 --> 01:36:12.650
Give Miina back! Miina!

01:36:12.780 --> 01:36:13.730
Wataru!

01:36:27.540 --> 01:36:30.570
That's inexcusable.
The Goddess must be evil to allow that.

01:36:31.740 --> 01:36:34.250
Wish it, Wataru.

01:36:34.900 --> 01:36:37.130
Wish for the Goddess to be destroyed.

01:36:38.780 --> 01:36:39.730
I...

01:36:40.540 --> 01:36:42.490
That's it, wish it.

01:36:44.020 --> 01:36:46.290
No! I don't want to!

01:36:47.020 --> 01:36:52.090
Why? Don't you want to save your mum?

01:36:57.260 --> 01:36:58.400
Mitsuru!

01:37:04.580 --> 01:37:05.560
I...

01:37:06.780 --> 01:37:10.890
I don't want to be the only one happy
by destroying others' happiness.

01:37:11.340 --> 01:37:15.650
Mitsuru burnt the forest,
massacred Vision's people and animals,

01:37:16.100 --> 01:37:20.610
to bring his sister back to life,
to change his destiny.

01:37:21.180 --> 01:37:25.730
But, at the end, he said it!
That he was wrong!

01:37:26.300 --> 01:37:28.970
It's because he wouldn't listen to me.

01:37:29.780 --> 01:37:32.080
But you, Wataru, are different.

01:37:33.060 --> 01:37:35.290
My dearest Wataru.

01:37:35.780 --> 01:37:39.970
Whatever happens, I will protect you.

01:37:40.580 --> 01:37:45.290
So please, destroy the Goddess.

01:37:45.420 --> 01:37:50.170
If you do that, then Vision and the mortal
world will become yours and mine.

01:37:51.020 --> 01:37:53.010
So wish it!

01:37:54.220 --> 01:37:57.410
No! You're wrong!

01:37:57.540 --> 01:38:02.450
Why? Even though
all your wishes will be granted?

01:38:02.620 --> 01:38:03.650
I don't want that!

01:38:03.860 --> 01:38:07.010
Why not? Why?

01:38:07.140 --> 01:38:12.810
Why? Even after all the times I rescued you!

01:38:17.900 --> 01:38:20.930
I was a goddess.

01:38:21.220 --> 01:38:26.240
I could have been the Goddess of Destiny.

01:38:26.620 --> 01:38:30.650
I thought that I could do it with Wataru.

01:38:31.420 --> 01:38:35.930
Wataru! Wataru! Wataru! Wataru!

01:38:42.500 --> 01:38:44.770
Wataru!

01:39:37.420 --> 01:39:39.410
This is Vision?

01:39:51.620 --> 01:39:53.050
The Kasara...

01:39:57.300 --> 01:40:02.890
When you see the Goddess of Destiny,
what are you going to wish for?

01:40:04.300 --> 01:40:05.250
Miina.

01:40:54.260 --> 01:40:55.290
Goddess!

01:40:57.780 --> 01:41:01.690
Take my hand and say your wish.

01:41:02.220 --> 01:41:05.690
Put your wish into my hand.

01:41:07.540 --> 01:41:08.490
Yes.

01:41:17.700 --> 01:41:19.410
Your wish is?

01:41:23.820 --> 01:41:24.770
My...

01:41:30.060 --> 01:41:31.040
My...

01:41:31.380 --> 01:41:33.610
Our wish is...

01:41:34.700 --> 01:41:35.810
Goddess,

01:41:36.180 --> 01:41:40.650
with your strength,
please remove the monsters in Vision.

01:41:41.980 --> 01:41:46.970
I can only grant your wish this once.

01:41:48.140 --> 01:41:49.410
There is no second wish.

01:41:50.140 --> 01:41:51.090
I know.

01:41:52.580 --> 01:41:56.690
If this wish is fulfilled,
your destiny in the mortal world

01:41:56.820 --> 01:41:59.250
will not change at all.

01:42:00.500 --> 01:42:05.360
Did you not come to Vision,
and face many obstacles,

01:42:05.780 --> 01:42:08.730
for a different wish?

01:42:09.100 --> 01:42:13.730
Yes. In the beginning,
it was to get my family back.

01:42:14.460 --> 01:42:18.610
But after coming to Vision
and making friends and journeying,

01:42:18.740 --> 01:42:20.450
I realized something.

01:42:20.820 --> 01:42:24.290
As there is joy and happiness
in one's destiny,

01:42:24.620 --> 01:42:28.730
there will be grief and misery.
It is impossible to avoid that.

01:42:28.980 --> 01:42:31.410
I cannot ask you to change my fate

01:42:31.540 --> 01:42:34.690
every time I come across grief or misery.

01:42:35.860 --> 01:42:38.970
When there is joy, there will be grief.

01:42:39.540 --> 01:42:42.570
Where there is happiness,
there will be misery.

01:42:43.380 --> 01:42:44.330
Yes.

01:42:44.580 --> 01:42:47.450
I will accept my own destiny,

01:42:47.580 --> 01:42:51.050
and make my own future.

01:42:51.780 --> 01:42:56.490
For the sake of my friends
who helped me realize that,

01:42:56.900 --> 01:42:59.530
please give this world a future.

01:43:01.500 --> 01:43:02.610
Brave One, Wataru!

01:43:03.380 --> 01:43:08.320
I will return you to the Earth
with that answer you found!

01:43:42.820 --> 01:43:44.250
What is this?

01:44:07.020 --> 01:44:09.480
The flowers are blooming!

01:44:09.620 --> 01:44:12.210
- Yes!
- Yes!

01:44:24.060 --> 01:44:26.690
Wataru, so this is your journey.

01:44:38.380 --> 01:44:40.090
Wataru!

01:44:42.580 --> 01:44:43.530
Wataru!

01:44:46.420 --> 01:44:50.450
Wataru, we saw what you did, your justice.

01:44:50.780 --> 01:44:54.210
Stupid Wataru! Ignoring your own wish!

01:44:54.340 --> 01:44:58.170
- Wataru!
- Wataru!

01:44:59.140 --> 01:45:02.090
Ki-Kima. Miina.

01:45:18.220 --> 01:45:20.680
Wataru!

01:45:21.060 --> 01:45:24.330
Damn it!
I don't care if you don't give good luck.

01:45:24.460 --> 01:45:28.410
So come back! Wataru!

01:45:28.620 --> 01:45:32.160
Wataru! Good-bye!

01:45:32.380 --> 01:45:34.530
Wataru!

01:45:40.980 --> 01:45:43.050
- Hurry up!
- Wait!

01:45:43.220 --> 01:45:45.170
Let's play dodgeball!

01:45:45.300 --> 01:45:46.360
Sure, why not?

01:45:46.700 --> 01:45:49.770
OMATSU BUILDING DEMOLITION WORK

01:45:57.180 --> 01:45:58.610
All right, laundry is finished!

01:45:58.900 --> 01:46:01.460
Mum, can you set the plates out?

01:46:01.660 --> 01:46:02.610
Okay!

01:46:05.100 --> 01:46:06.970
There are onions in it.

01:46:07.300 --> 01:46:10.650
None of that! You can't be picky.
You're a grown-up.

01:46:10.940 --> 01:46:12.210
All right.

01:46:14.260 --> 01:46:16.530
- Wataru!
- Sorry for making you wait!

01:46:17.580 --> 01:46:20.770
And so no one was able
to answer the question.

01:46:21.980 --> 01:46:23.890
Hey, you two are going to be late!

01:46:24.220 --> 01:46:25.280
You too, Mum!

01:46:26.540 --> 01:46:27.490
Bye!

01:46:28.460 --> 01:46:29.970
We're already in sixth grade!

01:46:30.220 --> 01:46:32.810
I bet Mitsuru would have been able
to answer it.

01:46:33.300 --> 01:46:35.490
Mitsuru? Who's that?

01:46:54.380 --> 01:46:57.490
Oh, yeah! I forgot.
There's a new kid coming in today.

01:46:57.660 --> 01:46:58.610
New kid?

01:47:00.220 --> 01:47:02.970
I'm sorry. You okay?

01:47:03.780 --> 01:47:04.890
Yeah. I'm fine!

01:47:05.580 --> 01:47:07.210
Wait, you are...

01:47:07.380 --> 01:47:08.330
Aya!

01:47:08.460 --> 01:47:09.730
Big brother!

01:47:11.300 --> 01:47:13.250
Didn't I say not to go off by yourself?
